  "body": "## What happens\n\nOn a clean `origin/main` at `fac6c8e8d22cb39bb0a4c18644b4ec1c4dbd2db6`, one `camcraft-ui --lib` test fails:\n\n`egui_app::rest_pocket_tests::rest_group_warns_and_refuses_incompatible_strategy_and_predrilled_on_apply`\n\n```\nthread '...rest_group_warns_and_refuses_incompatible_strategy_and_predrilled_on_apply' panicked at crates\\ui\\src\\egui_app\\rest_pocket_tests.rs:280:65:\nZigzag draft refusal\ntest result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 990 filtered out\n```\n\nCommand: `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- rest_group_warns_and_refuses_incompatible_strategy_and_predrilled_on_apply`. The test also fails alone.\n\n## Suspected cause\n\nBatch 16 merged PR #2037 (merge `9f247b741`, `fix(2d): clear Zigzag rest boundaries without wall cusps`, fixes #1490). That PR makes Zigzag legal for 2D rest machining. `rest_strategy(Zigzag)` now returns `Ok`. The UI test from #1815 still expects the old Zigzag refusal. The PR updated the motion and app tests, but not this UI test.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The test asserts the behaviour of #2037: Zigzag with rest machining shows no refusal, and Apply commits.\n- The test keeps a refusal assert for each refusal that still applies: the Adaptive strategy and pre-drilled entry.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib rest_pocket_tests` is green on the fix branch.\n",
